# Flutter rules

- Read `docs/FLUTTER_ARCHITECTURE.md` (and journey sections in `docs/USER_SCENARIOS.md` when changing UX).
- Preserve feature-first Clean Architecture: UI → Provider/ChangeNotifier → Repository → RemoteDataSource → Dio.
- Presentation must not import Dio, `http`, or Firebase packages.
- Keep Provider as primary state; do not replace with a new state-management pattern without an ADR.
- Wire new app-wide providers in both `AppDependencies` and `App`.
- Use `ApiConstants` paths; map snake_case via existing payload helpers.
- No mock/demo data layers.
- Localization via `L10n`; theme via existing `ThemeProvider` / palette.
- After Flutter code changes that affect architecture or API usage, update the matching docs in the same task.
- Prefer existing shared widgets under `lib/core/widgets/`.
